# Line endings in the files that the tests read.
#
# The engine tests read a fixture file and compare the bytes that come back.
# A Windows checkout converts a text file to CRLF by default. That conversion
# changes the bytes, so the test fails in a way that looks like a defect in a
# converter rather than a setting in the checkout.
#
# Pin the text files to LF on every platform. This is not a preference about
# editors. It is the condition under which the tests mean anything on Windows.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.mdx text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.astro text eol=lf

# Binary, and never converted.
#
# These are the fixture formats and the shipped binaries. A line ending
# conversion corrupts every one of them silently, and a corrupt fixture makes
# a passing test meaningless rather than making it fail.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.heic binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.wasm binary
*.onnx binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
